Ryujinx shader translator: every operand of every emitted SPIR-V instruction asks for its type, and each of those
calls ends in Module's type-declaration dictionary, whose key hash (DeterministicHashCode.Combine over the candidate
instruction's operands) is recomputed on every probe. The answers cannot change within one module, so hold the
scalar and vector types (and the four TypeS32/TypeU32/TypeFP32/TypeFP64 wrappers) in the context. The first request
for each still creates the type, in the same order, so the emitted module is byte-identical. The Ryujinx code in
the context lines is MIT.
